From a1d5d5de7da1aa77227f51d28d3d72f852c0977b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cline <cline@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:03:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add reel scheduling, page scraping and dashboard tooling to
 article-reels/

These four scripts plus the dashboard were living in the bengali-tip-cards
repo, in a folder that also held this repo's reel MP4s. That made one folder
contain two projects' tooling aimed at two different Facebook Pages. They
belong here, next to the reels they operate on.

Added under article-reels/:
- schedule-reels.py    - uploads the reels as scheduled (unpublished) posts
- scrape-page-posts.py - pulls posts/engagement from tracked Pages
- generate_dashboard.py - builds the offline dashboard.html
- fb-oauth.py          - mints a long-lived page token
- dashboard.css/js     - the dashboard's stylesheet and behaviour
- .reel-schedule-manifest.json, page-posts.json, sumona-posts.json,
  boho-posts.csv       - the current schedule and scraped data

Notes:
- No token is hardcoded. schedule-reels.py and scrape-page-posts.py had a
  fallback token baked in; it is gone, and both now read FB_PAGE_TOKEN (or
  --token) and exit with a clear message when it is missing. schedule-reels.py
  --dry-run still works without one.
- scrape-page-posts.py could not run at all: a stray "w" before the shebang
  made line 1 the expression `w`, so it died with NameError on every
  invocation. Removed.
- The generated dashboard.html is not committed (added to .gitignore); run
  generate_dashboard.py to produce it.
- README gained sections for scheduling, page tracking, the dashboard and
  tokens.

One thing left as-is: a re-run lays out slots from --start-date without
consulting the times the manifest already holds for other reels, so two reels
can end up sharing a publish minute.
